# SOC-001 — Malicious Document to PowerShell Attack

## Incident Overview

- Incident ID: SOC-001
- Severity: High
- Affected Host: PC-15
- User: Rahul
- Status: Contained / Under Investigation

## Executive Summary

A suspicious Microsoft Word document was opened by the user.
The document triggered PowerShell execution, which downloaded an
executable from an external IP address.

The downloaded executable was then executed and established an
outbound connection to the same external IP. Persistence was also
created through a Windows Registry Run Key.

The incident was classified as High severity because multiple
stages of a potential attack were observed.

## Attack Timeline

| Time | Event |
|---|---|
| 10:00:01 | User opened Salary_Revision.docx |
| 10:00:05 | winword.exe spawned powershell.exe |
| 10:00:07 | PowerShell executed with ExecutionPolicy Bypass and hidden window |
| 10:00:10 | PowerShell downloaded a.exe from 185.20.10.5 |
| 10:00:15 | a.exe appeared in C:\Users\Public\a.exe |
| 10:00:20 | a.exe connected to 185.20.10.5:443 |
| 10:00:30 | Registry Run Key persistence was created |

